# M4.29.2 staged hash-list transcription failure

Date: 2026-08-28

## Symptom

The second CI-approved payload was staged. Validation stopped on
`tu1nz_integrity_consolidation.sh` even though the calculated staged hash was
the correct committed value.

## Cause

The expected hash embedded manually in the operational validation command had
one transcribed character too many. The committed M4.29.2 manifest and staged
payload were not wrong.

## Impact

- installation from the second commit: not started;
- services: remain stopped;
- Control: unchanged;
- Adult Candidate: unchanged and never started.

## Resolution

Do not repeat a manually transcribed hash list. Stage the committed manifest
and have Python compare every staged payload file directly with the manifest's
artifact map. Require exactly eight matching installable artifacts before the
runtime-user check or installation.
